# Expo Bare (Bare on Mobile)

## Overview
Expo Bare refers to running Bare runtime inside a React Native/Expo app using `react-native-bare-kit` and `bare-pack` bundles. This lets mobile apps run P2P backends (Hypercore, Hyperswarm, QVAC) in a Bare worklet while the UI stays in React Native.

## Version Notes (read before bumping anything)

The Expo + Bare mobile stack is a **coupled set** — Expo SDK, React Native,
`react-native-bare-kit`, and `bare-pack` only have one validated combination
at a time. Bumping any single one of them risks breaking the worklet bundle
pipeline. See `core/verified-versions.mdc` → "Mobile (Expo + Bare)" for the
authoritative table.

Today's pinned set (last verified 2026-05-21):

| Package | Pinned | Anchor / why |
|---------|--------|--------------|
| `bare-pack` | `^1.5.1` | **Anchor.** `2.0.0` (Jan 2026) removed the `--target` CLI flag that our `build:bare` script uses. Do **not** bump to `2.x` until the generator switches the bundler invocation off `--target`. |
| `react-native-bare-kit` | `0.12.3` (exact) | **Required exact pin by `@qvac/sdk@0.11`.** Newer/older versions break the QVAC mobile worker bundle. |
| `expo` | `~54.0.33` | Pairs with `react-native@0.81.x`. SDK 55 / 56 ship `react-native@0.83` / `0.85`, neither validated against `bare-pack@1.5.1` + `react-native-bare-kit@0.12.3`. |
| `react-native` | `0.81.5` (exact) | Bound to Expo SDK 54. |
| Expo ecosystem (`expo-router`, `expo-build-properties`, `expo-file-system`, `expo-device`, `expo-linking`, `expo-splash-screen`, `expo-status-bar`, `react-native-safe-area-context`, `react-native-screens`) | matching `~5x.x.x` | All bound to Expo SDK 54. |

Historical context: reference apps (`qvac-workbench-mobile`, `qvac-health`)
still pin `react-native-bare-kit@^0.11.5`, so our `0.12.3` pin (forced by
`@qvac/sdk@0.11` peer dep) is already one step ahead. The next step — Expo
SDK 56 + `bare-pack@2.x` — is gated on upstream QVAC reference apps
migrating first.

## Installation
```bash
# Use the scaffold — never hand-install these. The scaffold pins every
# version against a validated combination. See `setup-mobile-app` skill.
us scaffold app -p expo-mobile -n <name> -f local-ai
```

## Quick Start
```bash
git clone https://github.com/holepunchto/bare-expo.git my-bare-app
cd my-bare-app
npm i
```

```bash
# Bundle Bare backend for iOS + Android. The `--target` flag is bare-pack 1.x
# only — drop to a bare-pack 2.x invocation when (and only when) the whole
# coupled set above is re-validated together.
npx bare-pack --target ios --target android --linked --out app/app.bundle.mjs backend/backend.mjs
```

## Core Concepts
- Worklet: `react-native-bare-kit` runs a Bare thread inside RN.
- Bundling: `bare-pack` produces a single bundle with native addon references.
- RPC bridge: `bare-rpc` over the Worklet IPC stream connects UI and backend.

## API Reference
- `Worklet.start(path, bundle, args)` to launch Bare.
- `bare-pack --target ios --target android --linked` for mobile bundles.
- `bare-rpc` request/response over IPC.

## Integration with Other Modules
- Hyperswarm/Hypercore run inside the Bare worklet for P2P networking.
- QVAC uses Bare for inference on mobile via Expo (physical device required).
- WDK uses `react-native-bare-kit` for crypto/network modules.

## Common Patterns
```js
// UI side
import { Worklet } from "react-native-bare-kit"
import RPC from "bare-rpc"

const worklet = new Worklet()
worklet.start("/app.bundle", bundle, [documentDirectory])
const rpc = new RPC(worklet.IPC, onRequest)
```

```js
// Bare backend side
import RPC from "bare-rpc"
const { IPC } = BareKit
const rpc = new RPC(IPC, onRequest)
```

## Pitfalls & Gotchas
- Android requires minSdkVersion 29+ and NDK alignment (Expo build props).
- Bundle with `--linked` to use prelinked native addons on mobile.
- QVAC LLM inference does not run on emulators; use physical devices.
- **Never bump `bare-pack` past `1.5.1`** until the generator switches off
  `--target` — the CLI flag was removed in `2.0.0` and builds will fail with
  `Unknown option '--target'` during `prestart` / `preios` / `preandroid`.
- **Never bump `react-native-bare-kit`** away from the exact version that
  the installed `@qvac/sdk` declares as its peer (currently `0.12.3` for
  `@qvac/sdk@0.11`). Caret ranges silently install a newer pre-1.0 minor
  and break the SDK's mobile worker bundle with cryptic native errors.
- **Bump Expo SDK only as a coordinated set.** The Expo monorepo pins each
  SDK to one specific `react-native` major. Mixing SDK 54 with RN 0.85
  (SDK 56's RN) is not a supported configuration.

